In /app/frontend/src/index.css, add an explicit exception rule for the destructive AlertDialog action so the 'Sil' button stays white on red. Recommended one-liner addition after the current exception block:

[role="dialog"] .text-primary-foreground, [role="dialog"] .text-primary-foreground *,
[role="alertdialog"] .text-primary-foreground, [role="alertdialog"] .text-primary-foreground * { color: hsl(var(--primary-foreground)) !important; -webkit-text-fill-color: hsl(var(--primary-foreground)) !important; }

Or alternatively target the destructive bg directly:

[role="alertdialog"] .bg-red-600, [role="alertdialog"] .bg-red-600 *, [role="alertdialog"] .bg-destructive, [role="alertdialog"] .bg-destructive * { color: #ffffff !important; -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff !important; }

After fix, re-verify by opening any delete AlertDialog and asserting getComputedStyle of the 'Sil' button color === near-white (rgb(250, 250, 250) or rgb(255, 255, 255)).
